      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Today the historic Claiborne Wharf serves as a county‑owned boat launch, while a jetty built for the passenger ferry is leased from the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.claibornemd.org/about-claiborne",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Baltimore & Eastern Shore Railroad finished a rail line from Claiborne to Easton in 1890, allowing travelers to continue on to Ocean City.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claiborne%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The former United Methodist Church, now Village Hall since 2010, preserves a historic building that once served as a community center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
